  "equipment_type": "Sensor (CO2 probe)",
  "applies_to": "GMP251 probe in Modbus RTU mode, user guide M211799EN-N.",
  "summary": "The GMP251 is a Vaisala CARBOCAP probe for percent-level CO2 (incubators, life science). Over RS-485 it is a Modbus RTU slave. This map covers the CO2 and temperature readings, the compensation registers, serial settings and status/error registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": "Error code register needs probe firmware 1.4.3 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "GMP251 and GMP80P User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M211799EN-N",
    "revision_date": "2026-11",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M211799EN-N/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 131-140 (Tables 62-70)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All values are holding registers read with function 03 and written with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and the 32-bit error code put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB); the guide confirms this with a worked read frame (bytes D4 7A 43 E8 = 465.66 ppm).",
    "Missing data returns quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (integer) instead of an exception.",
    "Power-up compensation registers are stored in EEPROM (about 30000 writes); write the volatile registers for frequent updates.",
    "The same guide covers GMP80P, which is not included here; the register list in the Modbus chapter is written for the GMP251 probe.",
    "The guide lists the CO2 registers in ppm."
  ],
